From a06f0744976e3e6e0928e4ca1f3e2d7ac917048f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:19:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 127/140] hydra: split lights for lobe multipliers, shadow
 colour and shadowless lights

Cycles scales a light as a whole. A light whose diffuse and specular
multipliers differ, or that has a shadow colour, is now split over twins -
copies of the light and its object: one per lobe group at that lobe's
multiplier, and for a shadow colour c each with shadows at 1 - c and
without at c. A camera-only twin shows a visible light at full strength.

BSDF rays stop at the first light they hit, so of coplanar parts only the
first with shadows takes part in MIS; the others, and any light without
shadows, are reached by light sampling alone. That also fixes
shadow:enable = 0, whose shadows stayed half dark (K-87).

Sockets are copied by value: Node::set_value takes an array over from its
source, which left the original light without its shader.
